From 0fc4420f819262bea744c063f1ddba655b85ede7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vitaly Lipatov <lav@etersoft.ru>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 11:41:44 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 33/37] ASoC: wcd938x: bind TCL firmware nodes and clean
 aggregate IRQ state

The WCD9385 aggregate and its RX/TX SoundWire devices are supplied by
software nodes during ACPI boot. OF phandle matching alone cannot
assemble them, and IRQ-domain objects must not outlive the codec binding
that owns their callbacks.

Validate the firmware port maps, resolve the RX/TX node references, and
match components through those references. Add IRQ cleanup and failure
unwind for the aggregate. Recognize the explicitly named TCL test
aggregate so its external providers own regulator/reset setup instead of
requiring an OF topology. This is still board-specific integration: it
does not supply a generic ACPI regulator description, validated headset
thresholds or proven microphone routing.
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd938x-sdw.c |  29 +++++-
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd938x.c     | 159 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 166 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

